   558	    is exactly ``Σ_{s,v} (U_{s,v} − 1)·P^p_{s,v}``, so the ratio between the
   559	    two forms is the load-weighted mean occupancy — measured at 2.28x for
   560	    100 users and 1.41x for 20, which is what identified the defect.
   561	
   562	    The damage was not the scale.  The extra term rises monotonically with
   563	    occupancy and sits in ``r1``'s **denominator**, so "a busier beam is
   564	    less efficient" — which is ``r3``'s job.  A constant offset would not
   565	    move an argmax; a load-dependent one makes the first and third
   566	    objectives inseparable and voids the reading of ``Ω = (0.5, 0.3, 0.2)``.
