   228	Because active-beam and satellite vectors have variable cardinality, the NPZ
   229	uses fixed K/S dimensions equal to the largest complete vector in this shard
   230	(and Kc/Sc for controls) and stores the corresponding counts; unused slots
   231	are filled with -1 for keys/IDs and 0 for powers.  The JSON sidecar metadata
   232	records K/S/Kc/Sc and sentinel rules.
   233	
   234	For a simpler implementation, the same arrays may be emitted per anchor in
   235	`anchor-<phase>.npz`; the index must then contain one relative path and hash
   236	per anchor.  A fit worker must support either only after the schema version is
   237	explicitly raised.  Version 1 uses one world-level NPZ.
   238	
   239	## Recomputability and safety rules
   240	
   241	1. JSON is canonical ASCII (`sort_keys`, compact separators, no NaN/Infinity).
   242	2. NPZ is loaded with `allow_pickle=False`; object arrays are forbidden.
   243	3. Arrays are hashed with dtype, shape, and C-order bytes.  No digest-only
   244	   representation is accepted as a fit input.
   245	4. The fit worker reconstructs `C3View`, `LCSRSAnchorCapture`, topology,
   246	   `LCSRSPairTargets`, `LCSRSAnchorSurface`, and `LCSRSAnchorRecord` from the
   247	   sidecar and independently verifies every runtime digest before fitting.
   248	5. Profile rows retain all 32 draws and all 00/10/01/11 profiles.  Partial,
   249	   no-close, negative, unsupported, reference, and masked records are not
   250	   silently removed; only the frozen surface class mask excludes them from
   251	   the learner loss.
   252	6. The artifact does not contain TEST rows, learner updates, a post-selection
   253	action, or a sign-filtered subset.  It is development evidence only.
